---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';

const path = '/compare/klaviyo-vs-omnisend';
const title = 'Klaviyo vs Omnisend for Shopify SMS: 14 Products and Migration Options';
const desc = 'A practical Shopify SMS comparison: Klaviyo and Omnisend against 12 adjacent products, including retired Yotpo messaging, with pricing caveats and a four-flow pilot.';

const tools = [
  { name: 'Klaviyo', fit: 'Deep Shopify events, complex segmentation, and teams that will maintain a data model.', profile: 'Klaviyo offers Shopify-connected profiles, event-based segmentation and email/SMS flows. Shortlist it when product, order and customer properties must drive different journey branches. The benefit is reusable customer context; the pilot must show that the required fields actually arrive and remain usable.', detail: 'Have the retention owner build a segment from an order event and a customer property, then edit its exclusion while a profile is waiting. Record what happens to that queued profile. Price the expected active profiles and destination-specific messaging separately.', best: 'Data-heavy retention teams', pros: 'Shopify event depth; advanced segmentation; broad ecosystem', cons: 'Field mapping, profile hygiene and queue edits need an owner', price: 'Free entry tier; paid pricing varies by active profiles and SMS usage', url: 'https://www.klaviyo.com/pricing' },
  { name: 'Omnisend', fit: 'Teams evaluating a shared email, SMS and push workspace', profile: 'Omnisend documents email, SMS and web push within its automation builder, including prebuilt ecommerce journeys. That shared workspace is useful when a small team wants to inspect channel steps together. It does not establish a faster implementation than Klaviyo for your store.', detail: 'Build the same purchase exit and conditional channel path in both candidates. In Omnisend, inspect whether an ineligible SMS step skips, waits or invokes a permitted fallback. In Klaviyo, inspect the corresponding flow behavior. Compare the work needed to explain and safely edit each path.', best: 'Combined-channel workflow evaluation', pros: 'Email/SMS/push in one workflow; ecommerce templates', cons: 'Channel eligibility, exclusions and plan limits still need validation', price: 'Free tier; paid tiers vary by contacts, sends, and channels', url: 'https://www.omnisend.com/pricing/' },
  { name: 'Postscript', fit: 'SMS-first Shopify teams that need campaigns, recovery, and replies.', profile: 'Postscript remains a candidate for Shopify SMS acquisition, campaigns and conversations. Its current launch page also announces Postscript Email, identity resolution, configurable attribution and migration tools. Email is a positive evaluation option rather than a reason to assume a second provider is required.', detail: 'The launch page invites merchants to join the Email waitlist. Confirm access, migration scope and the exact email workflows in your proposed account before consolidating. If retaining another email sender, assign one recovery owner and prove purchase and opt-out handoffs instead of assuming either architecture prevents collisions.', best: 'Shopify SMS with an Email evaluation path', pros: 'SMS focus; Shopify-oriented flows; reply handling', cons: 'Email access and migration scope need account confirmation', price: 'Usage-based; inspect current plan and message rates', url: 'https://postscript.io/pricing' },
  { name: 'Attentive', fit: 'Larger DTC brands with acquisition volume and a budget for managed SMS.', profile: 'Attentive belongs on an enterprise shortlist when acquisition, consent capture, lifecycle orchestration, and operational support are material parts of the program. The decision is usually about scale and service model, not finding the lowest monthly app fee.', detail: 'Request the current scope of SMS and email products, acquisition tools and support in the proposal. Ask for written message, carrier, onboarding, data-retention and cancellation terms. Compare operator effort as well as invoice totals; vendor case studies are not a forecast for this store.', best: 'Enterprise SMS acquisition and governance', pros: 'Enterprise support; SMS acquisition tooling; broad integrations', cons: 'Confirm service scope, onboarding effort and contract obligations', price: 'Custom quote; request a complete cost model', url: 'https://www.attentive.com/pricing' },
  { name: 'Yotpo Email & SMS', fit: 'Historical migration context; excluded from new messaging selection', profile: 'Yotpo Email & SMS is a retired messaging product, not a current alternative to Klaviyo or Omnisend. Its lifecycle notice says the SMS application is decommissioned and its dashboard and background services are inactive. The official migration announcement scheduled full Email and SMS deprecation for December 31, 2025.', detail: 'Yotpo Reviews and Loyalty continue as separate products; their availability does not restore the retired messaging suite. For a migration, reconcile available exports, consent provenance, suppressions and historical attribution with the replacement sender. Verify any Reviews or Loyalty data bridge separately.', best: 'Retired messaging: migration context only', pros: 'Reviews and Loyalty remain separate evaluation options', cons: 'Retired Email/SMS suite cannot be shortlisted for new sends', price: 'No current messaging price recommendation; scope replacement costs', url: 'https://email-and-sms.yotpo.com/' },
  { name: 'Sendlane', fit: 'Growing DTC brands wanting guided ecommerce automation and migration help.', profile: 'Sendlane is a candidate for teams that want ecommerce-focused automation but prefer a more guided buying and onboarding process. Test how quickly an operator can build the four core flows and how clearly revenue, suppression, and SMS cost are exposed.', detail: 'Compare its proposed ecommerce automation and migration assistance against the same four flows, not an assumed entry-price premium. Ask which events, sends, destinations and support tasks are included, and identify who repairs a failed sync after onboarding.', best: 'Guided DTC retention programs', pros: 'Ecommerce focus; migration support; cross-channel workflows', cons: 'Confirm onboarding scope and equivalent usage in a written proposal', price: 'Request current contact, sending, SMS and support terms', url: 'https://www.sendlane.com/pricing' },
  { name: 'Brevo', fit: 'Cost-aware teams that need email volume, transactional mail, and optional SMS.', profile: 'Brevo offers marketing email and transactional sending, with SMS subject to destination and account eligibility. Its Shopify integration should be evaluated on the actual customer and order fields required by the journey rather than an assumption that a general platform has shallow commerce data.', detail: 'Do not treat a low email price as a low total retention cost. Shopify event depth, template work, SMS country coverage, carrier fees, and reporting effort can change the calculation. Confirm whether the exact SMS use case is supported in the store’s target countries.', best: 'Budget-conscious email plus selective SMS', pros: 'Email-volume economics; transactional options; broad channel basics', cons: 'Prove required Shopify events and destination-specific SMS eligibility', price: 'Free entry; paid plans and SMS credits depend on volume and country', url: 'https://www.brevo.com/pricing/' },
  { name: 'Privy', fit: 'Stores whose biggest bottleneck is permissioned list capture.', profile: 'Privy belongs before a sophisticated SMS comparison when the store is losing potential subscribers at the popup and checkout stages. Its value is capture mechanics: forms, offers, and basic campaigns that turn traffic into an addressable audience.', detail: 'Capture is not consent by default. Inspect disclosure, promised purpose, source and timestamp transfer into the sender. Evaluate current email and SMS workflows as well as forms; do not assume capture tooling either supplies or excludes the lifecycle branching you require.', best: 'Popup and SMS list growth', pros: 'Capture-first workflow; accessible for smaller teams; Shopify fit', cons: 'Capture conversion and downstream suppression need separate checks', price: 'Free entry and paid tiers vary by contacts or usage', url: 'https://www.privy.com/pricing' },
  { name: 'Recart', fit: 'Mobile-first cart and browse recovery programs.', profile: 'Recart is worth testing when the specific question is whether mobile reminders recover more high-intent carts than the current email flow. Its narrower focus can be useful for a team that wants a defined experiment instead of migrating every lifecycle message.', detail: 'Do not infer its full channel or lifecycle scope from this recovery use case. Request current product access, destinations and service scope. Use a shared suppression map and a randomized eligible holdout before treating attributed recovery revenue as incremental sales.', best: 'Mobile cart recovery tests', pros: 'Focused recovery use case; mobile-first approach; quick experiment scope', cons: 'Recovery attribution can overlap other senders', price: 'Plan and message terms vary; model usage plus discounts', url: 'https://recart.com/' },
  { name: 'Firepush', fit: 'Web push evaluation alongside a separately governed messaging program', profile: 'The current Firepush site focuses on Shopify web push, including welcome, cart, stock and price reminders. This is a concrete reason to test browser notifications for opted-in shoppers. It is not evidence that a new account can activate an email/SMS suite.', detail: 'Legacy email and SMS descriptions do not resolve current new-account access. Obtain written confirmation before relying on those channels; no retirement date is asserted here. Test push permission, reminder expiry and purchase cancellation, and coordinate frequency with whichever platform owns email and SMS.', best: 'Browser-push reminders', pros: 'Push templates; stock and price reminders; Shopify focus', cons: 'New-account email/SMS availability remains unresolved', price: 'Verify current push allowance and paid sending terms', url: 'https://getfirepush.com/' },
  { name: 'Shopify Email', fit: 'Native, simple email for stores not yet ready for a full SMS stack.', profile: 'Shopify Email provides an email baseline close to the commerce admin. Use it to evaluate native campaign creation and automation before deciding whether broader orchestration warrants migration. This entry concerns the email product, not the availability of every Shopify messaging service.', detail: 'Use it to compare the cost and effort of welcome, post-purchase, and basic promotional email before adding SMS complexity. Check current send allowances and eligibility in the Shopify admin; native availability and commercial terms can change.', best: 'Native starter email', pros: 'Low setup friction; Shopify-native context; clear baseline', cons: 'Prove the required journey branches and cross-app exclusions', price: 'Availability and allowances depend on the Shopify plan and current terms', url: 'https://www.shopify.com/email' },
  { name: 'Mailchimp', fit: 'Teams migrating from a general email platform with familiar campaign workflows.', profile: 'Mailchimp can make sense when the team values familiar email creation, broad integrations, and a gradual move from newsletters into basic automation. It belongs in the comparison when the alternative is an existing general-purpose stack, not only when shopping for SMS.', detail: 'Shopify event depth, SMS availability, contact billing, and automation limits require an account-specific check. Treat the app as a candidate for the email control arm unless the exact SMS and consent workflow is confirmed for the store’s market.', best: 'Familiar email operations', pros: 'Known editor; broad ecosystem; accessible campaign workflow', cons: 'Check contact accounting, automation access and data synchronization', price: 'Free and paid tiers vary by contacts and features', url: 'https://mailchimp.com/pricing/' },
  { name: 'Sequenzy', fit: 'Email automation with Shopify data and an optional SMS add-on', profile: 'Sequenzy documents Shopify customer, order and product sync, commerce email flows and an optional US/Canada SMS add-on. That makes a combined workflow worth evaluating when destinations fit; a dedicated companion SMS sender is an architecture choice, not a requirement.', detail: 'Prove the actual Shopify trigger, purchase exit and channel eligibility in the proposed account. If keeping a separate sender, document the handoff and cancellation behavior. Email pricing based on sends and unlimited contacts should be compared with normal and peak volumes; it does not establish lower total cost for every store.', best: 'Send-based email and optional SMS', pros: 'Shopify sync; email automation; optional US/Canada SMS', cons: 'Confirm destination coverage, add-on access and workflow fit', price: 'Current plan and usage terms should be checked before a forecast', url: 'https://sequenzy.com/pricing' },
  { name: 'ActiveCampaign', fit: 'Teams needing CRM-style automation beyond straightforward Shopify campaigns.', profile: 'ActiveCampaign enters the shortlist when lifecycle messaging must connect with CRM stages, sales follow-up, or more general automation than a Shopify-only store needs. It can be powerful when those extra objects are real requirements.', detail: 'Additional flexibility can mean additional integration and governance work. Prove Shopify order, product, consent, and suppression data in the pilot instead of assuming a CRM integration provides the same ecommerce event depth as a native specialist.', best: 'CRM-linked lifecycle programs', pros: 'Automation flexibility; CRM context; wide integration surface', cons: 'CRM stages and commerce events need explicit mapping and ownership', price: 'Tiered pricing varies by contacts and features; verify current quote', url: 'https://www.activecampaign.com/pricing' },
];

const faqs = [
  { question: 'Is Klaviyo or Omnisend better for Shopify SMS?', answer: 'Evaluate both against your actual events, segmentation and maintenance requirements. Verify current email, SMS and push availability, destinations and plan eligibility independently; a module name or suite label does not establish channel scope. Build the same journeys and compare safe operation rather than assuming data depth or faster launch determines the winner.' },
  { question: 'Are the prices in this comparison guarantees?', answer: 'No. They are buying-model notes, not quotes. Contact tiers, message volume, carrier fees, regional availability, add-ons, contracts, and plan names change. Use the linked official pricing or sales pages and request a written estimate for your list and send mix.' },
  { question: 'Should a Shopify store use both email and SMS?', answer: 'Use a purpose and channel map before combining email and SMS. Confirm permission for the intended message, then recheck current opt-out, suppression, purchase and subscription state at dispatch. Assign sender and queue ownership to each journey, cancel stale messages after conversion and deduplicate replayed events. A documented fallback must respect current eligibility; permission for one channel does not authorize another.' },
];
