    <article class="prose-shopify mt-12 max-w-4xl">
<h2>Proposed identity and handover fixtures</h2>
<p>Use two checkouts from one identified shopper, a guest checkout later associated with that shopper, and a replay of the same event ID. Record customer, checkout and order identifiers, occurrence time and receipt time in each platform. Require one intended entry per event, cancellation of the purchased checkout, and no accidental cancellation of the other checkout. Test a late purchase event and an opt-out while a reminder waits. These are proposed fixtures; no account tests or delivery results are reported here.</p>
<p>Name the retention owner for each journey, the integration owner for missing fields and the support owner for replies. Before switching, pause old entry points, inventory queued reminders, decide which to cancel or drain, then activate the replacement with a rollback plan. Preserve channel-specific permission evidence and suppression state. Never replay the entire migration history as new recovery events.</p>
<h2>Implementation pilot: four flows, fourteen days</h2>
<p>Do not migrate the whole account to decide between Klaviyo and Omnisend. Create a test segment with documented consent and build the same four flows: welcome, abandoned cart, post-purchase, and winback. Use identical message goals, discount ceilings, quiet hours, recent-purchase exclusions, gift-buyer treatment, and email/SMS collision rules. Keep promotional broadcasts out of the pilot.</p>
<ol>
<li>Days 1–2: export consent source, timestamp, country, phone status, and suppression fields; verify Shopify product and order events.</li>
<li>Days 3–5: build the four flows and preview every branch on a real device or controlled test profile.</li>
<li>Days 6–10: send to a limited eligible cohort; keep a holdout and record delivered messages, fees, discounts, replies, opt-outs, and orders.</li>
<li>Days 11–14: estimate contribution margin and record operator hours; inspect failed triggers, duplicate sends, and stale catalog data before choosing.</li>
</ol>
<p>Treat the fourteen-day heading as an illustrative planning window, not a deadline or proof of sufficient experiment power. Before any activation, assign sender and queue ownership, cancel superseded messages and test replay deduplication. A conversion must update other eligible queues promptly. Choose from safe-edit and maintenance evidence; randomize an eligible holdout with a defined outcome window and uncertainty reporting before calling attributed orders incremental lift.</p>
</article>

    <div class="mt-12 card overflow-x-auto">
